      "text": [
        " سُوقٍ مِنْ أَسْوَاقِ اَلْجَبَلِ أَ يَسْأَلُ عَنْ ذَكَاتِهِ إِذَا كَانَ اَلْبَائِعُ مُسْلِماً غَيْرَ عَارِفٍ قَالَ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ «عَلَيْكُمْ أَنْ تَسْأَلُوا عَنْهُ إِذَا رَأَيْتُمُ اَلْمُشْرِكِينَ يَبِيعُونَ ذَلِكَ وَ إِذَا رَأَيْتُمُوهُمْ يُصَلُّونَ فَلاَ تَسْأَلُوا عَنْهُ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.792 - Ismail ibn Isa asked Abu Al-Hasan al-Ridha about leather and fur items purchased from a market in the mountain regions: Should a person inquire about their source of slaughter (i.e., whether it was properly done) if the seller is a Muslim but not a known believer?\nHe (as) replied: \"You should inquire if you see that the sellers are polytheists selling those items. But if you see them performing prayer, then you do not need to ask”."
        ]
      }
